        {
          "id": "53e55d0c-eef6-33dd-859a-c56df1329f33",
          "content": {
            "id": "53e55d0c-eef6-33dd-859a-c56df1329f33",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Autonomous vehicles are driving more aggressively, and maybe that's needed",
            "description": "<p>While Waymo's self-driving cars \u2014 which is a subsidiary of Google parent company Alphabet (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GOOG\">GOOG</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GOOGL\">GOOGL</a>) \u2014 are found to be involved in fewer accidents than human drivers in the metro areas it operates in, according to Semafor, the autonomous vehicles appear to be engaging <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/lifestyle/cars/waymo-self-driving-cars-san-francisco-7868eb2b?gaa_at=eafs&gaa_n=AWEtsqf7586R-LWJme-wp1jIyTcYnCydjOObpbh76IhFwNPX4d5Iykrpv8NHkZ0hI7s%3D&gaa_ts=693c53ad&gaa_sig=Y4FN1czwG6zuzFIAcQ1DPYCsbJ8j77PEXbcWffcrb4qnH0b2Ow2TRC9vKh1rqeTrYvIcu4o9lxV2yZ94Qubv-g%3D%3D\">in more aggressive driving</a> in several videos that have gone viral.</p>\n<p>University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Associate Director of the Center for Autonomy associate professor Katherine Driggs-Campbell helps break down the behavior shift in Waymo vehicles, whether this is all safer or necessary for autonomous vehicle learning,</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
